{"id": "EUVD-2026-57616", "enisaUuid": "75818e58-e8b8-3ac4-8fb7-6b905bb4519e", "description": "A flaw was found in the provider-credential-controller component of multicluster-engine (MCE). An attacker with specific permissions on the hub cluster, and knowledge of a prior credential value, could exploit an authorization bypass vulnerability. By manipulating `copiedFrom` labels, the attacker could intercept newly rotated provider credentials, leading to unauthorized information disclosure. This allows access to sensitive credentials that should otherwise be protected.", "datePublished": "2026-08-12T20:46:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T19:41:06", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59556", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59557", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59558", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59559", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59579", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59593", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-19130", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2512105"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-19130", "GHSA-3vwx-g7ch-f3wg"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6c53cdb6-d3d6-330c-bed1-c43dbe1fb312", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.17", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786664288"}, {"id": "703e6a99-ab44-31ee-a7ff-9f3d4e622d37", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787176716"}, {"id": "91bc56d5-6c9c-356e-a971-1bd3acaf7c71", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.6", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787260821"}, {"id": "a528ee54-ed29-3eb2-88c2-0a64a625304b", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}